From 9a7b4803583cbeb9a8edf2de17154ac13be2811f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Ville=20Kivela=CC=88?= <vkivela@hotmail.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 19:38:52 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] extensions: connect an extension to a native messaging
 host

runtime.connectNative was refused by the base messaging delegate, so an
extension could not reach a program outside the browser. 1Password's
desktop integration is native messaging, and Bitwarden's desktop unlock
is the same channel.

Chrome's host manifest parser, process launcher, launch context and
message port dispatcher compile with their own includes rewritten and two
changes: the manifest is looked up through QtWebEngine's own path keys,
because the range Chrome's chrome_paths uses is the range QtWebEngine
already uses for its storage paths, and NativeMessageHost::Create passes
no profile directory, because a host that wants to start a connection of
its own by relaunching the browser has no browser to relaunch here.

The per-user directory is this application's own, so a host installed for
it is found without the application naming a path. Which hosts may be
launched stays the application's decision: a host manifest already names
the extensions it answers, and QtWebEngine loads no extension the
application did not hand it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
